--   * leg 1 has a via at 0 -448 -18.5; leg 1 pull group 22 has an approach at -24 -536 29.7 and leg 3 pull group 3 one
--     at 0 -448 -18.5, splitting the 0 -448 and -21.33 -533.33 seams that path-check refuses at the raw row
--     coordinates (the run leader sends 1-decimal orders, which pass; the plan points keep both checks green).
-- Server replay (path-check and plan-check's server walk, at the run leader's 1-decimal `cmd move` orders):
--   before: leg 0 steps 52, 53 and 54 refused from the lead's -45.3 -404 31.5 (2 x unreachable, 1 x no-progress);
--   after: 0 refused of 298 moves over the whole plan (pulls move nobody) and 0 of 64 from step 51's point.
-- Plan check: 1 of 371 points fails (the known leg 2 pull group 10 look point, a lone Smolderthorn Berserker on a z -7
-- ledge: the mapping walk's); 12 detours unchanged (leg 0 groups 8 and 18; leg 1 groups 9, 14 and 16; leg 2 groups 11,
-- 14, 17, 21, 22, 26 and 29); 84 run-leader hop notices.
-- What the rows cannot carry: the level band, the hire composition, the 16 `fleers`, the patrol phases, the 4 rares'
-- kill_first 9217, Urok Doomhowl (summoned by GO_CHALLENGE_UROK), Gizrul the Slavener (10268, no spawn row), the
-- Rookery eggs and the doors (UBRS-side).
--
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- lower_blackrock_spire: map 229, 7 legs, 420 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'lower_blackrock_spire';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'lower_blackrock_spire';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'lower_blackrock_spire';

-- Dungeon bosses of map 229 for the commander telemetry's boss rank (see 20261021114931_world.sql): the seven boss
-- steps' entries, names from Turtle's own world data (sql/base creature_template; all rank 1 or the rank-3 NPC bosses
-- 9236 and 9568, so the telemetry would call them 'e'). Entry-scoped on purpose: another plan's map-229 rows
-- (upper_blackrock_spire, a raid on the same map) survive. The rares 9217, 9218, 9219, 9718 and 10376 and Mor
-- Grayhoof 16080 are not seeded.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (229) AND `entry` IN (9196, 9236, 9237, 10596, 9736, 10220, 9568);
